Veyra milestone suggestions
===========================

Current milestone
-----------------
- M0–M6 foundation, interaction, workspace, multi-artboard and Component work is independently VERIFIED.
- Active work is `milestone.md` M7 — Vector Authoring, Multi-Selection & Grouping UX.
- M7 must preserve `QUALITY.md`: editor-only UX stays out of the minimal playback runtime, authored geometry remains canonical, and no second evaluator/model is introduced.

Queued work after M7
--------------------
1. Resume master `plan.md` with View Models / Data Binding / Property Groups / enums / converters / lists.
2. Continue into full layered state-machine parity and later Rive feature families in plan order.
3. Translate the checked-in `deep-research-report (6).md` into later bounded milestones for Lottie JSON + dotLottie interoperability, masks/mattes, Motion Tokens/slots, compatibility analysis, import/export fidelity and modular runtimes. Do not silently collapse these into generic Rive features.
4. Introduce a semantic shortcut/keymap profile system (Veyra / Rive / Lottie-AE / Custom) once M7's semantic editor-command layer is stable.
5. Add bundle-size/performance regression tooling when a compiled/distributable runtime target exists; enforce the budgets in `QUALITY.md` rather than optimizing by deleting parity features.
6. Build a compatibility analyzer before broad interchange export: exact / approximate / bake / rasterize / reject, with no silent feature loss.
7. Revisit the paused headless Node API/CLI only after the browser/editor contracts being reused are settled.

Longer-term lightweight/runtime principles
------------------------------------------
- Keep `.veyra` editable source distinct from a future compact `.vyr` runtime artifact.
- Use one evaluator semantics across editor preview and runtime.
- Prefer compiler stripping, dead-scene elimination, asset/geometry deduplication, font subsetting, dirty evaluation and settled-state sleeping over feature removal.
- Keep optional runtime modules such as text, audio, scripting, accessibility, advanced effects and debugging separable from the minimal vector/timeline core.
- Port to Rust/WASM/native only after evaluator/file contracts are sufficiently frozen and compatibility tests can prove semantic equivalence.

Guardrails
----------
- `milestone.md` remains the only active implementation milestone.
- `plan.md` remains the authoritative product roadmap; `QUALITY.md` is the permanent non-functional engineering contract.
- Future work stays here until the current milestone is independently accepted.
- Stable IDs and human display names remain separate contracts.
- UI convenience must not introduce a second mutation model or bypass the canonical control plane/Store validation boundary.
- No interchange exporter may silently drop unsupported Veyra features.
